> Cast rays to detect block and entity hits, with voxel-accurate collisions.

name: Raycast
slug: bookshelf-raycast
version: 5.0.0
tags: runtime

$run = #[command(slash="forbidden",empty="forbidden")] string
$provider = #[id(registry="function",tags="allowed")] string

$blocks = $provider > [block provider](hitbox.md#block-providers) of the blocks the ray hits, such as `#bs.hitbox:get_block/collision`: without it, the ray goes through blocks
$entities = $provider > [entity provider](hitbox.md#entity-providers) of the entities the ray hits, such as `#bs.hitbox:get_entity/sized`: without it, the ray goes through entities
$selector = string > selector arguments the entities must match, such as `tag=my_pack.target`

$hit = success > whether a block or an entity stops the ray


feature function cast
  > Cast a ray and check if it hits a block or an entity.
  authors: Aksiome
  contributors: Bafy78
  created: 2023/10/09 1.20.2
  updated: 2026/10/13 26.3

  context position > origin of the ray
  context rotation > direction of the ray
  context dimension > dimension of the ray
  input arguments: {
    blocks?: $blocks
    entities?: $entities
    selector?: $selector
    max_distance?: number @ 0..2047 > distance the ray travels at most, 16 by default
    on_block?: $run > command to run at the block the ray hits, aligned to the grid
    on_entity?: $run > command to run as and at the entity the ray hits
    on_entry?: $run > command to run at the point where the ray enters the nearest box it hits
  }
  output $hit


feature function pierce
  > Cast a ray that goes through every block and entity it hits, until a command stops it.
  authors: Aksiome
  contributors: Bafy78
  created: 2026/10/25 26.3
  updated: 2026/10/25 26.3

  context position > origin of the ray
  context rotation > direction of the ray
  context dimension > dimension of the ray
  input arguments: {
    blocks?: $provider
    entities?: $entities
    selector?: $selector
    max_distance?: number @ 0..2047 > distance the ray travels at most, 16 by default
    on_block?: $run > command to run at each block the ray hits, aligned to the grid: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_entity?: $run > command to run as and at each entity the ray hits: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_entry?: $run > command to run at each point where the ray enters a box, nearest first: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_exit?: $run > command to run at each point where the ray leaves a box, right after its `on_entry`: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
  }
  output success > whether a command stops the ray


feature predicate face/bottom
  > Check if the ray enters the box it hits by its bottom face. Use it in a command of the ray.
  authors: Aksiome
  created: 2026/10/13 26.3
  updated: 2026/10/13 26.3

  output success > whether the bottom face is hit


